      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 608,
        "height": 544,
        "content": "## Read invoices on a DGX Spark\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow lets a user upload an invoice through a form, converts the uploaded image/file to base64, and sends it to a DGX Spark-hosted chat completion endpoint for OCR. It then sends the recognized text to a Qwen model on the same Spark endpoint to extract structured invoice fields. The extracted fields are normalized and displayed back to the user in a form.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the upload form to accept the invoice file types you expect, such as images or PDFs.\n- Ensure the extract-from-file node is reading the correct uploaded file property and producing base64 output for the OCR request.\n- Replace `http://<spark-ip>:4000/v1/chat/completions` with the reachable DGX Spark endpoint address in both HTTP Request nodes.\n- Configure any required API authentication headers or tokens for the local Spark inference server.\n- Verify the OCR and Qwen extraction prompts/models match the models available on the DGX Spark service.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the OCR prompt, field-extraction prompt, and Set node fields to capture the invoice fields your organization needs, such as purchase order number, tax ID, line items, or payment terms."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
